/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A flexible drive has three parts: a driving pulley or sprocket on the input shaft, a driven one on the output shaft, and one continuous member wrapped round both.
   - The members divide by how they grip.
   - Against a gear pair the trade is clear.
   - Leather is the oldest belt material and still the textbook reference.
   - Cotton canvas, woven into a heavy cloth called duck and bonded with rubber, makes the common rubber flat belt.
   - High-strength belts use synthetic cords.
   - A flat belt is a stack of layers.
   - A flat belt must be joined into a loop.
   - V-belts are moulded endless, with a trapezoidal cross-section and a layer of tension cord just under the top face.
   - Tc is the centrifugal tension in N, which pulls on the belt even when it carries no load; m is the mass per metre length in kg/m; v is belt speed in m/s; ρ is belt material density in kg/m³; b is belt width in m; t is belt thickness in m.
*/
