/* book: lead: A V-belt sits in a grooved pulley and wedges into it. The wedge raises the effective friction from μ to about μ / sin β, roughly three times, so the drive grips with a short centre distance and small pulleys. The price is that one belt carries only a few kilowatts; the drive is rated as a number of standard belts. V-belts run pumps, compressors, fans and machine tools, including many Indian worksh */
