/* book exam traps: Using the full groove angle in sin β. For 2β = 38°, sin 19° = 0.326, not sin 38° = 0.616; the wrong value roughly halves μ′. | Forgetting the service factor. The belts must carry Pd = FaP, not the motor power P. | Using millimetres in v = πdN/60. Put d in metres, or the speed comes out 1000 times too large. | Rounding the number of belts down. 4.19 means 5 belts; 4 belts carry only 8.60 kW against 9.0 kW. | Using the flat-belt ratio eμθ for a V-belt. The V-belt exponent is μθ/sin β: 4.54 instead of 1.64 in worked example 2. */
